/* NotchOTP — English localization.
 *
 * Every key is a French literal copied verbatim from the sources, in the exact form the
 * compiler emits it (`%@` where a value is inserted, `%lld` where an integer is); the
 * localizer looks them up by exact match, so a key is never retyped or reformulated.
 * Comments say where each string is shown. The last section holds the keys whose
 * English is the French itself, listed so the table covers every key the app looks up.
 *
 * Absent on purpose: literals that are identifiers, log messages or demo fixture data
 * rather than copy. The plural forms are at the end of the file, next to a note saying
 * where the branch is written.
 */

